  "answer": "The multi-region disaster recovery strategy for the financial institution is structured as follows: 1) Objectives set at RTO < 15 minutes and RPO = 0 (Zero Data Loss) to comply with Basel III/PCI-DSS. 2) Deployment of an Active-Active cloud architecture across paired regions. 3) Usage of synchronous replication for mission-critical databases with periodic cross-region consistency validation. 4) Implementation of Global Server Load Balancing (GSLB) with latency-based routing and health-check-triggered failover. 5) Automated orchestration via Infrastructure-as-Code (Terraform) and CI/CD pipelines for failover/failback. 6) Integration of immutable, air-gapped snapshots for ransomware resilience. 7) Quarterly 'Game Day' simulations and continuous chaos testing using tools like AWS Fault Injection Simulator. 8) Unified observability stack providing real-time telemetry across regions.",
